,"name":"影月 零","avatarUrl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/864634?s=64\u0026v=4","__isNode":"User"}]}}],"pinnedIssueComment":null,"__isIssueOrPullRequest":"Issue","isPinned":false,"viewerCanDelete":false,"viewerCanTransfer":false,"viewerCanConvertToDiscussion":false,"viewerCanLock":false,"timelineItems":{"totalCount":18,"beforeFocusCount":0,"afterFocusCount":0,"pageInfo":{"hasNextPage":true,"hasPreviousPage":false,"startCursor":"Y3Vyc29yOnYyOpPPAAABbbZxkNgAqTU0MDY2MDIxOQ==","endCursor":"Y3Vyc29yOnYyOpPPAAABcinNOZgAqTYzMDQ1NzE4Mg=="},"edges":[{"cursor":"Y3Vyc29yOnYyOpPPAAABbbZxkNgAqTU0MDY2MDIxOQ==","node":{"__typename":"IssueComment","id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU0MDY2MDIxOQ==","createdAt":"2019-10-10T16:12:39Z","url":"https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js/issues/17706#issuecomment-540660219","isHidden":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":null,"databaseId":540660219,"viewerDidAuthor":false,"issue":{"id":"MDU6SXNzdWU1MDUxNTQ4NzE=","author":{"__typename":"User","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4MjQ4MTQ=","login":"0b5vr"},"number":17706,"locked":false,"databaseId":505154871},"author":{"__typename":"User","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDgzNjg=","login":"donmccurdy","avatarUrl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1848368?u=ff978bf21f6fa05d34dc58a832528f6948988660\u0026v=4","profileUrl":"https://github.com/donmccurdy","name":"Don McCurdy"},"authorAssociation":"COLLABORATOR","viewerCanDelete":false,"viewerCanMinimize":false,"viewerCanUnminimize":false,"viewerCanReport":false,"viewerCanReportToMaintainer":false,"viewerCanBlockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanUnblockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanBlockPersonally":false,"viewerCanUnblockPersonally":false,"viewerCanPin":false,"viewerCanUnpin":false,"viaApp":null,"showSpammyBadge":false,"createdViaEmail":false,"authorToRepoOwnerSponsorship":null,"viewerCanReadUserContentEdits":true,"lastEditedAt":null,"lastUserContentEdit":null,"pinnedBy":null,"body":"\u003e Currently, we are letting depthWrite: true for every material that is being loaded from GLTFLoader.\r\n\r\nI think we came to the conclusion that https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js/issues/13889 was a modeling issue. Can you give other examples of models that require `depthWrite: true`? My impression is that without it, we handle transparency correctly roughly as often as babylonjs, although either may succeed and fail in different situations.\r\n\r\n\u003e And glTF spec does not specify how we must set our depth write, even in non-normative sections, since the use of glTF is not restricted to the traditional realtime rasterizer.\r\n\r\nglTF files are meant to be renderable by realtime rasterizers, but even with that, I'm not sure whether it's true that a majority of implementations set `depthWrite: false` for models with the \"BLEND\" alpha mode.\r\n\r\n***\r\n\r\nI'm OK with considering a change here, but (1) I don't know whether `depthWrite: false` is the right change, as opposed to (for example) a different sorting algorithm, and (2) if there is a change I don't think it should be in GLTFLoader alone. The glTF format does not specify depthWrite for alpha transparency because we don't think there's a single correct/consensus answer. GLTFLoader uses three.js defaults to be consistent with user expectations, so if we change anything here, it should probably be the three.js defaults – there's nothing particularly different about alpha transparency in glTF vs FBX, the same limitations apply.","bodyHTML":"\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eCurrently, we are letting depthWrite: true for every material that is being loaded from GLTFLoader.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eI think we came to the conclusion that \u003ca class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"315369405\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js/issues/13889\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mrdoob/three.js/issues/13889/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js/issues/13889\"\u003e#13889\u003c/a\u003e was a modeling issue. Can you give other examples of models that require \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003edepthWrite: true\u003c/code\u003e? My impression is that without it, we handle transparency correctly roughly as often as babylonjs, although either may succeed and fail in different situations.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eAnd glTF spec does not specify how we must set our depth write, even in non-normative sections, since the use of glTF is not restricted to the traditional realtime rasterizer.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eglTF files are meant to be renderable by realtime rasterizers, but even with that, I'm not sure whether it's true that a majority of implementations set \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003edepthWrite: false\u003c/code\u003e for models with the \"BLEND\" alpha mode.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eI'm OK with considering a change here, but (1) I don't know whether \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003edepthWrite: false\u003c/code\u003e is the right change, as opposed to (for example) a different sorting algorithm, and (2) if there is a change I don't think it should be in GLTFLoader alone. The glTF format does not specify depthWrite for alpha transparency because we don't think there's a single correct/consensus answer. GLTFLoader uses three.js defaults to be consistent with user expectations, so if we change anything here, it should probably be the three.js defaults – there's nothing particularly different about alpha transparency in glTF vs FBX, the same limitations apply.\u003c/p\u003e","bodyVersion":"40f3ac2f3c15c325a9ca3de4317a577eee6afb4433c26d058297a506ca47338f","viewerCanUpdate":false,"repository":{"id":"MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnk1NzYyMDE=","name":"three.js","owner":{"__typename":"User","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk3MDg4","login":"mrdoob","url":"https://github.com/mrdoob"},"isPrivate":false,"viewerCanCreateIssues":false,"slashCommandsEnabled":false,"nameWithOwner":"mrdoob/three.js","databaseId":576201},"reactionGroups":[{"content":"THUMBS_UP","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":1,"nodes":[{"__typename":"User","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NDYzNA==","login":"Kagetsuki","name":"影月 零","avatarUrl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/864634?s=64\u0026v=4"}]}},{"content":"THUMBS_DOWN","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"LAUGH","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"HOORAY","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"CONFUSED","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"HEART","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"ROCKET","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"EYES","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}}]}},{"cursor":"Y3Vyc29yOnYyOpPPAAABbbZxsBgBqjI3MDMzMzkzNzQ=","node":{"__typename":"LabeledEvent","id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDI3MDMzMzkzNzQ=","databaseId":2703339374,"createdAt":"2019-10-10T16:12:47Z","actor":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDgzNjg=","avatarUrl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1848368?s=64\u0026u=ff978bf21f6fa05d34dc58a832528f6948988660\u0026v=4","login":"donmccurdy","profileResourcePath":"/donmccurdy","__typename":"User","name":"Don McCurdy"},"label":{"id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNzU4Mjc=","archivedAt":null,"nameHTML":"Suggestion","name":"Suggestion","color":"ffffcf","description":null},"intent":null}},{"cursor":"Y3Vyc29yOnYyOpPPAAABbbbcbFAAqTU0MDcwNTg0MQ==","node":{"__typename":"IssueComment","id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU0MDcwNTg0MQ==","createdAt":"2019-10-10T18:09:22Z","url":"https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js/issues/17706#issuecomment-540705841","isHidden":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":null,"databaseId":540705841,"viewerDidAuthor":false,"issue":{"id":"MDU6SXNzdWU1MDUxNTQ4NzE=","author":{"__typename":"User","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4MjQ4MTQ=","login":"0b5vr"},"number":17706,"locked":false,"databaseId":505154871},"author":{"__typename":"User","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4MjQ4MTQ=","login":"0b5vr","avatarUrl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7824814?u=c1e255ca0125d2b76005840c4185e4e3fdf3208f\u0026v=4","profileUrl":"https://github.com/0b5vr","name":"0b5vr"},"authorAssociation":"COLLABORATOR","viewerCanDelete":false,"viewerCanMinimize":false,"viewerCanUnminimize":false,"viewerCanReport":false,"viewerCanReportToMaintainer":false,"viewerCanBlockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanUnblockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanBlockPersonally":false,"viewerCanUnblockPersonally":false,"viewerCanPin":false,"viewerCanUnpin":false,"viaApp":null,"showSpammyBadge":false,"createdViaEmail":false,"authorToRepoOwnerSponsorship":null,"viewerCanReadUserContentEdits":true,"lastEditedAt":"2019-10-10T18:13:57Z","lastUserContentEdit":{"id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDI5MTE0OTUzNA==","editor":{"__typename":"User","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4MjQ4MTQ=","url":"https://github.com/0b5vr","login":"0b5vr"}},"pinnedBy":null,"body":"Yes that is pretty expected and reasonable answer, thank you @donmccurdy -san!\r\nI think I need more examples of actual model and implementations.\r\n\r\nOur current implementation that let end developers to decide whether or not use depth write for any materials (using `.depthWrite`) is more flexible, but make it consistent over the entire Three.js as BabylonJS does also sounds good, I can't judge about it, we need more opinion imo.","bodyHTML":"\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eYes that is pretty expected and reasonable answer, thank you \u003ca class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/donmccurdy/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/donmccurdy\"\u003e@donmccurdy\u003c/a\u003e -san!\u003cbr\u003e\nI think I need more examples of actual model and implementations.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eOur current implementation that let end developers to decide whether or not use depth write for any materials (using \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003e.depthWrite\u003c/code\u003e) is more flexible, but make it consistent over the entire Three.js as BabylonJS does also sounds good, I can't judge about it, we need more opinion imo.\u003c/p\u003e","bodyVersion":"942d558e00ce9892233e96a4d0b52b7520bf048017f6d5aff273261e971175a4","viewerCanUpdate":false,"repository":{"id":"MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnk1NzYyMDE=","name":"three.js","owner":{"__typename":"User","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk3MDg4","login":"mrdoob","url":"https://github.com/mrdoob"},"isPrivate":false,"viewerCanCreateIssues":false,"slashCommandsEnabled":false,"nameWithOwner":"mrdoob/three.js","databaseId":576201},"reactionGroups":[{"content":"THUMBS_UP","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":1,"nodes":[{"__typename":"User","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NDYzNA==","login":"Kagetsuki","name":"影月 零","avatarUrl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/864634?s=64\u0026v=4"}]}},{"content":"THUMBS_DOWN","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"LAUGH","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"HOORAY","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"CONFUSED","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"HEART","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"ROCKET","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"EYES","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}}]}},{"cursor":"Y3Vyc29yOnYyOpPPAAABbu5kTMgAqTU2Mzg3ODAwMw==","node":{"__typename":"IssueComment","id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU2Mzg3ODAwMw==","createdAt":"2019-12-10T05:59:41Z","url":"https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js/issues/17706#issuecomment-563878003","isHidden":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":null,"databaseId":563878003,"viewerDidAuthor":false,"issue":{"id":"MDU6SXNzdWU1MDUxNTQ4NzE=","author":{"__typename":"User","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4MjQ4MTQ=","login":"0b5vr"},"number":17706,"locked":false,"databaseId":505154871},"author":{"__typename":"User","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NDYzNA==","login":"Kagetsuki","avatarUrl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/864634?v=4","profileUrl":"https://github.com/Kagetsuki","name":"影月 零"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","viewerCanDelete":false,"viewerCanMinimize":false,"viewerCanUnminimize":false,"viewerCanReport":false,"viewerCanReportToMaintainer":false,"viewerCanBlockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanUnblockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanBlockPersonally":false,"viewerCanUnblockPersonally":false,"viewerCanPin":false,"viewerCanUnpin":false,"viaApp":null,"showSpammyBadge":false,"createdViaEmail":false,"authorToRepoOwnerSponsorship":null,"viewerCanReadUserContentEdits":true,"lastEditedAt":null,"lastUserContentEdit":null,"pinnedBy":null,"body":"We've essentially run into this issue and I think we may have a very specific example. We have a semi transparent material under a mostly transparent material and it displays fairly well in babylon, but in three.js we have two scenarios:\r\n1. Default of depthWrite: true does not calculate the transparency of the material behind the other transparent material and is either culling it or giving it a very high alpha or something (left is three, right is babylon):\r\n![defaults comparison](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/864634/70498673-7d373c80-1b5a-11ea-98bc-a6a6235d6e69.png)\r\n2. Setting depthWrite to false seems to completely ruin materials:\r\n![depthWrite disabled](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/864634/70498827-02225600-1b5b-11ea-8242-dedfe5b52e11.png)\r\n\r\nHere's the glb of the model we're testing (we can provide the original Blend file if anyone wants it).\r\n[HumanEye-V2(concept).zip](https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js/files/3943221/HumanEye-V2.concept.zip)\r\n\r\nFor us it would be preferable if the display was like babylon by default - as the babylon version is very close to what we're looking for and it seems to have a high[er] compatibility with the Blender (2.81) glTF exporter. For others this may of course not be the case, but I feel like with so much effort being put into the Blender exporter by members of the Khronos Group(♥) it may be a better reference.?\r\n\r\nIf there's anything we can do to help with this issue please let me know.","bodyHTML":"\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eWe've essentially run into this issue and I think we may have a very specific example. We have a semi transparent material under a mostly transparent material and it displays fairly well in babylon, but in three.js we have two scenarios:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col dir=\"auto\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDefault of depthWrite: true does not calculate the transparency of the material behind the other transparent material and is either culling it or giving it a very high alpha or something (left is three, right is babylon):\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003ca target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/864634/70498673-7d373c80-1b5a-11ea-98bc-a6a6235d6e69.png\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/864634/70498673-7d373c80-1b5a-11ea-98bc-a6a6235d6e69.png\" alt=\"defaults comparison\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSetting depthWrite to false seems to completely ruin materials:\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003ca target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/864634/70498827-02225600-1b5b-11ea-8242-dedfe5b52e11.png\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/864634/70498827-02225600-1b5b-11ea-8242-dedfe5b52e11.png\" alt=\"depthWrite disabled\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eHere's the glb of the model we're testing (we can provide the original Blend file if anyone wants it).\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js/files/3943221/HumanEye-V2.concept.zip\"\u003eHumanEye-V2(concept).zip\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eFor us it would be preferable if the display was like babylon by default - as the babylon version is very close to what we're looking for and it seems to have a high[er] compatibility with the Blender (2.81) glTF exporter. For others this may of course not be the case, but I feel like with so much effort being put into the Blender exporter by members of the Khronos Group(♥) it may be a better reference.?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eIf there's anything we can do to help with this issue please let me know.\u003c/p\u003e","bodyVersion":"4053cafec013a646091e324f8fec9dbd684cd82f18d7c9b0bb3255e868992f73","viewerCanUpdate":false,"repository":{"id":"MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnk1NzYyMDE=","name":"three.js","owner":{"__typename":"User","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk3MDg4","login":"mrdoob","url":"https://github.com/mrdoob"},"isPrivate":false,"viewerCanCreateIssues":false,"slashCommandsEnabled":false,"nameWithOwner":"mrdoob/three.js","databaseId":576201},"reactionGroups":[{"content":"THUMBS_UP","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"THUMBS_DOWN","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"LAUGH","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"HOORAY","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"CONFUSED","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"HEART","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"ROCKET","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"EYES","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}}]}},{"cursor":"Y3Vyc29yOnYyOpPPAAABbzEbgiAAqTU2ODM1NDUyMA==","node":{"__typename":"IssueComment","id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU2ODM1NDUyMA==","c