ocusCount":0,"pageInfo":{"hasNextPage":false,"hasPreviousPage":true,"startCursor":"Y3Vyc29yOnYyOpPPAAABbbbcbFAAqTU0MDcwNTg0MQ==","endCursor":"Y3Vyc29yOnYyOpPPAAABcioF4YAAqTYzMDQ3OTA0MA=="},"edges":[{"cursor":"Y3Vyc29yOnYyOpPPAAABbbbcbFAAqTU0MDcwNTg0MQ==","node":{"__typename":"IssueComment","id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU0MDcwNTg0MQ==","createdAt":"2019-10-10T18:09:22Z","url":"https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js/issues/17706#issuecomment-540705841","isHidden":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":null,"databaseId":540705841,"viewerDidAuthor":false,"issue":{"id":"MDU6SXNzdWU1MDUxNTQ4NzE=","author":{"__typename":"User","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4MjQ4MTQ=","login":"0b5vr"},"number":17706,"locked":false,"databaseId":505154871},"author":{"__typename":"User","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4MjQ4MTQ=","login":"0b5vr","avatarUrl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7824814?u=c1e255ca0125d2b76005840c4185e4e3fdf3208f\u0026v=4","profileUrl":"https://github.com/0b5vr","name":"0b5vr"},"authorAssociation":"COLLABORATOR","viewerCanDelete":false,"viewerCanMinimize":false,"viewerCanUnminimize":false,"viewerCanReport":false,"viewerCanReportToMaintainer":false,"viewerCanBlockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanUnblockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanBlockPersonally":false,"viewerCanUnblockPersonally":false,"viewerCanPin":false,"viewerCanUnpin":false,"viaApp":null,"showSpammyBadge":false,"createdViaEmail":false,"authorToRepoOwnerSponsorship":null,"viewerCanReadUserContentEdits":true,"lastEditedAt":"2019-10-10T18:13:57Z","lastUserContentEdit":{"id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDI5MTE0OTUzNA==","editor":{"__typename":"User","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4MjQ4MTQ=","url":"https://github.com/0b5vr","login":"0b5vr"}},"pinnedBy":null,"body":"Yes that is pretty expected and reasonable answer, thank you @donmccurdy -san!\r\nI think I need more examples of actual model and implementations.\r\n\r\nOur current implementation that let end developers to decide whether or not use depth write for any materials (using `.depthWrite`) is more flexible, but make it consistent over the entire Three.js as BabylonJS does also sounds good, I can't judge about it, we need more opinion imo.","bodyHTML":"\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eYes that is pretty expected and reasonable answer, thank you \u003ca class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/donmccurdy/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/donmccurdy\"\u003e@donmccurdy\u003c/a\u003e -san!\u003cbr\u003e\nI think I need more examples of actual model and implementations.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eOur current implementation that let end developers to decide whether or not use depth write for any materials (using \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003e.depthWrite\u003c/code\u003e) is more flexible, but make it consistent over the entire Three.js as BabylonJS does also sounds good, I can't judge about it, we need more opinion imo.\u003c/p\u003e","bodyVersion":"942d558e00ce9892233e96a4d0b52b7520bf048017f6d5aff273261e971175a4","viewerCanUpdate":false,"repository":{"id":"MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnk1NzYyMDE=","name":"three.js","owner":{"__typename":"User","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk3MDg4","login":"mrdoob","url":"https://github.com/mrdoob"},"isPrivate":false,"viewerCanCreateIssues":false,"slashCommandsEnabled":false,"nameWithOwner":"mrdoob/three.js","databaseId":576201},"reactionGroups":[{"content":"THUMBS_UP","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":1,"nodes":[{"__typename":"User","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NDYzNA==","login":"Kagetsuki","name":"影月 零","avatarUrl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/864634?s=64\u0026v=4"}]}},{"content":"THUMBS_DOWN","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"LAUGH","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"HOORAY","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"CONFUSED","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"HEART","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"ROCKET","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"EYES","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}}]}},{"cursor":"Y3Vyc29yOnYyOpPPAAABbu5kTMgAqTU2Mzg3ODAwMw==","node":{"__typename":"IssueComment","id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU2Mzg3ODAwMw==","createdAt":"2019-12-10T05:59:41Z","url":"https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js/issues/17706#issuecomment-563878003","isHidden":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":null,"databaseId":563878003,"viewerDidAuthor":false,"issue":{"id":"MDU6SXNzdWU1MDUxNTQ4NzE=","author":{"__typename":"User","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4MjQ4MTQ=","login":"0b5vr"},"number":17706,"locked":false,"databaseId":505154871},"author":{"__typename":"User","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NDYzNA==","login":"Kagetsuki","avatarUrl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/864634?v=4","profileUrl":"https://github.com/Kagetsuki","name":"影月 零"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","viewerCanDelete":false,"viewerCanMinimize":false,"viewerCanUnminimize":false,"viewerCanReport":false,"viewerCanReportToMaintainer":false,"viewerCanBlockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanUnblockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanBlockPersonally":false,"viewerCanUnblockPersonally":false,"viewerCanPin":false,"viewerCanUnpin":false,"viaApp":null,"showSpammyBadge":false,"createdViaEmail":false,"authorToRepoOwnerSponsorship":null,"viewerCanReadUserContentEdits":true,"lastEditedAt":null,"lastUserContentEdit":null,"pinnedBy":null,"body":"We've essentially run into this issue and I think we may have a very specific example. We have a semi transparent material under a mostly transparent material and it displays fairly well in babylon, but in three.js we have two scenarios:\r\n1. Default of depthWrite: true does not calculate the transparency of the material behind the other transparent material and is either culling it or giving it a very high alpha or something (left is three, right is babylon):\r\n![defaults comparison](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/864634/70498673-7d373c80-1b5a-11ea-98bc-a6a6235d6e69.png)\r\n2. Setting depthWrite to false seems to completely ruin materials:\r\n![depthWrite disabled](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/864634/70498827-02225600-1b5b-11ea-8242-dedfe5b52e11.png)\r\n\r\nHere's the glb of the model we're testing (we can provide the original Blend file if anyone wants it).\r\n[HumanEye-V2(concept).zip](https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js/files/3943221/HumanEye-V2.concept.zip)\r\n\r\nFor us it would be preferable if the display was like babylon by default - as the babylon version is very close to what we're looking for and it seems to have a high[er] compatibility with the Blender (2.81) glTF exporter. For others this may of course not be the case, but I feel like with so much effort being put into the Blender exporter by members of the Khronos Group(♥) it may be a better reference.?\r\n\r\nIf there's anything we can do to help with this issue please let me know.","bodyHTML":"\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eWe've essentially run into this issue and I think we may have a very specific example. We have a semi transparent material under a mostly transparent material and it displays fairly well in babylon, but in three.js we have two scenarios:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col dir=\"auto\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDefault of depthWrite: true does not calculate the transparency of the material behind the other transparent material and is either culling it or giving it a very high alpha or something (left is three, right is babylon):\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003ca target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/864634/70498673-7d373c80-1b5a-11ea-98bc-a6a6235d6e69.png\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/864634/70498673-7d373c80-1b5a-11ea-98bc-a6a6235d6e69.png\" alt=\"defaults comparison\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSetting depthWrite to false seems to completely ruin materials:\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003ca target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/864634/70498827-02225600-1b5b-11ea-8242-dedfe5b52e11.png\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/864634/70498827-02225600-1b5b-11ea-8242-dedfe5b52e11.png\" alt=\"depthWrite disabled\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eHere's the glb of the model we're testing (we can provide the original Blend file if anyone wants it).\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js/files/3943221/HumanEye-V2.concept.zip\"\u003eHumanEye-V2(concept).zip\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eFor us it would be preferable if the display was like babylon by default - as the babylon version is very close to what we're looking for and it seems to have a high[er] compatibility with the Blender (2.81) glTF exporter. For others this may of course not be the case, but I feel like with so much effort being put into the Blender exporter by members of the Khronos Group(♥) it may be a better reference.?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eIf there's anything we can do to help with this issue please let me know.\u003c/p\u003e","bodyVersion":"4053cafec013a646091e324f8fec9dbd684cd82f18d7c9b0bb3255e868992f73","viewerCanUpdate":false,"repository":{"id":"MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnk1NzYyMDE=","name":"three.js","owner":{"__typename":"User","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk3MDg4","login":"mrdoob","url":"https://github.com/mrdoob"},"isPrivate":false,"viewerCanCreateIssues":false,"slashCommandsEnabled":false,"nameWithOwner":"mrdoob/three.js","databaseId":576201},"reactionGroups":[{"content":"THUMBS_UP","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"THUMBS_DOWN","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"LAUGH","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"HOORAY","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"CONFUSED","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"HEART","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"ROCKET","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"EYES","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}}]}},{"cursor":"Y3Vyc29yOnYyOpPPAAABbzEbgiAAqTU2ODM1NDUyMA==","node":{"__typename":"IssueComment","id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU2ODM1NDUyMA==","createdAt":"2019-12-23T04:54:44Z","url":"https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js/issues/17706#issuecomment-568354520","isHidden":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":null,"databaseId":568354520,"viewerDidAuthor":false,"issue":{"id":"MDU6SXNzdWU1MDUxNTQ4NzE=","author":{"__typename":"User","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4MjQ4MTQ=","login":"0b5vr"},"number":17706,"locked":false,"databaseId":505154871},"author":{"__typename":"User","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDgzNjg=","login":"donmccurdy","avatarUrl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1848368?u=ff978bf21f6fa05d34dc58a832528f6948988660\u0026v=4","profileUrl":"https://github.com/donmccurdy","name":"Don McCurdy"},"authorAssociation":"COLLABORATOR","viewerCanDelete":false,"viewerCanMinimize":false,"viewerCanUnminimize":false,"viewerCanReport":false,"viewerCanReportToMaintainer":false,"viewerCanBlockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanUnblockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanBlockPersonally":false,"viewerCanUnblockPersonally":false,"viewerCanPin":false,"viewerCanUnpin":false,"viaApp":null,"showSpammyBadge":false,"createdViaEmail":false,"authorToRepoOwnerSponsorship":null,"viewerCanReadUserContentEdits":true,"lastEditedAt":null,"lastUserContentEdit":null,"pinnedBy":null,"body":"@Kagetsuki the problem visible in your third image comes from setting `depthWrite=false` on _all_ materials. If you set the option only on the transparent materials, you'll get a reasonable result.\r\